    <bpmn:process id="W_W598" name="W598. Wholesale Pricing &amp; Quotation Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Reseller requests quotation; new customer tier assessment; price list update cycle; government procurement RFQ; project-based pricing request
Frequency: ~80–120 quotations/month; tier assessments quarterly; price list updates monthly or upon cost change
Volume: ~100–150 active resellers across 4 wholesale tiers (Bronze/Silver/Gold/Platinum); trade accounts represent ~30% of revenue (PHP ~18.7B annually); ~15–20 government procurement quotations/year; ~30–40 project-based quotations/year
Owner: B2B Sales Manager
Participants: B2B Sales Manager, Sales Representative, Category Manager (A for below-threshold pricing), VP Merchandising (A for government/project pricing), Finance Analyst (R for margin validation), Credit Analyst (R for customer tier assessment), B2B Support Representative
Source: workflow W598 — Wholesale Pricing &amp; Quotation Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W598_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W598_Lane1" name="Credit Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W598_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W598_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W598_Lane2" name="B2B Sales Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W598_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W598_Lane3" name="Sales Representative">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W598_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W598_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W598_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W598_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W598_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W598_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W598_Lane5" name="Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W598_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W598_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W598_Start7" name="Reseller requests quotation; new customer tier assessment; price list update cycle…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W598_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W598_Task8" name="Customer tier assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer tier assessment: for each active reseller, quarterly tier review — (a) system pulls trailing 12-month purchase volume per reseller; (b) compare actual volume to tier threshold: Bronze &lt;PHP 5M, Silver PHP 5–15M, Gold PHP 15–30M, Platinum &gt;PHP 30M; (c) if reseller has moved to a higher tier: notify B2B Sales Manager for upgrade — apply new tier pricing to all future orders; (d) if reseller has dropped below tier threshold: notify for downgrade review — Sales Manager assesses whether drop is temporary (e.g., customer between projects) or permanent; temporary drops get 1-quarter grace period before downgrade; (e) tier change documented in customer master per W508; (f) for new resellers: assign initial tier based on projected annual volume declared during onboarding per W145; re-assess after first 90 days
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst / B2B Sales Manager
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: 15 min/reseller/quarter (~25 hours/quarter for ~100 resellers)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W598_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W598_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W598_Task9" name="Price list generation/confirmation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Price list generation/confirmation: monthly, B2B Sales Manager reviews wholesale price lists — (a) system generates updated wholesale price list by tier: SRP × (1 − tier discount %) for each active SKU in wholesale-eligible categories; (b) highlight SKUs with cost changes since last month (from W85 product costing) — verify that wholesale margin remains above minimum threshold per tier: Bronze minimum margin 8%, Silver 7%, Gold 6%, Platinum 5%; (c) highlight SKUs where wholesale price crosses a psychological price point (e.g., PHP 1,000, PHP 5,000) — minor adjustment may improve competitiveness; (d) flag SKUs where current promotional pricing (W13) is lower than wholesale tier pricing — apply &quot;whichever is lower&quot; rule or exclude from promo per category policy; (e) publish updated price list to B2B portal and punchout catalog per W283
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager / Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W598_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W598_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W598_Task10" name="Quotation creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quotation creation: Sales Representative creates B2B quotation in response to customer request — (a) customer requests quotation for specific items, quantities, and delivery requirements; (b) Sales Rep enters quotation in ERP: item lines with quantities, delivery address, requested delivery date; (c) system auto-prices items based on customer&#x27;s assigned tier; (d) Sales Rep adds delivery terms: (i) ex-DC pickup (customer arranges transport — no delivery charge), (ii) BuildRight delivery to customer site (delivery charge based on distance and weight per W52/W62B rates), (iii) cross-dock to customer&#x27;s designated location; (e) quotation validity: standard 30 days; for volatile commodities (cement, steel): 7 days; for government procurement: per bid validity requirement (typically 60–90 days); (f) Sales Rep reviews quotation totals and sends to customer via B2B portal or email
Responsible (R): Sales Representative
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: 20–30 min per quotation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W598_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W598_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W598_Task11" name="Margin validation against threshold">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Margin validation against threshold: system performs real-time margin check as quotation is created — (a) for each line item: calculate margin = (quotation price − landed cost per W85) / quotation price; (b) compare to minimum margin threshold per tier; (c) for individual items below threshold: system flags line with warning — &quot;Margin below minimum threshold for this tier&quot;; (d) for total quotation margin: if overall margin is below 4% (floor margin), system blocks quotation submission and requires override approval; (e) margin report attached to quotation for approver visibility
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W598_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W598_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W598_Task12" name="Approval for below-threshold pricing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Approval for below-threshold pricing: if quotation contains items below minimum margin threshold — (a) Sales Rep documents reason for below-threshold pricing: (i) competitive match (competitor offered lower price — attach evidence), (ii) strategic account retention (risk of losing customer to competitor), (iii) volume commitment (customer commits to higher volume in exchange for lower price), (iv) new customer acquisition (introductory pricing for first 3 orders), (v) government procurement (mandated pricing per bid requirements); (b) approval routing: below Bronze/Silver threshold → B2B Sales Manager approves; below Gold/Platinum threshold → Category Manager approves; any quotation with overall margin &lt;4% → Category Manager + Finance Manager joint approval; (c) government procurement quotations: VP Merchandising approval required for all bids — pricing may be below normal thresholds per government contract economics (volume certainty, payment terms)
Responsible (R): Sales Representative / B2B Sales Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager / VP Merchandising
Duration: 10–15 min per below-threshold quotation (plus approval wait time)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W598_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W598_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W598_Task13" name="Quotation validity management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quotation validity management: system tracks quotation lifecycle — (a) active quotations: not yet expired, not yet converted to order; (b) quotation expiry alerts: 5 days before expiry, system alerts Sales Rep to follow up with customer; (c) expired quotations: auto-close with &quot;Lost — No Response&quot; status if not converted; (d) quotation revision: if customer requests changes (quantity, items, delivery terms), Sales Rep creates revised quotation (versioned — V1, V2, V3); revised quotation resets validity period; (e) for volatile commodity quotations (7-day validity): system sends daily reminder to Sales Rep starting day 3
Responsible (R): System / Sales Representative
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min per follow-up</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W598_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W598_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W598_Task14" name="Order conversion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Order conversion: customer accepts quotation — (a) Sales Rep converts quotation to Sales Order in ERP; (b) system validates: quotation still within validity period, items still in stock at DC, customer credit limit not exceeded per W145; (c) if all validations pass: Sales Order created with quotation pricing locked (price protection for validity period); (d) if stock issue: system checks alternative DCs or suggests delivery split (partial now, balance on replenishment); (e) if credit limit exceeded: Sales Rep coordinates with Credit Analyst per W145 for temporary credit limit increase or split delivery; (f) converted quotation triggers fulfillment per W146 (bulk) or standard order fulfillment per W11/W19
Responsible (R): Sales Representative / System
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: 10–15 min per conversion</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W598_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W598_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W598_Task15" name="Post-sale price variance analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Post-sale price variance analysis: monthly, Finance Analyst reviews wholesale pricing performance — (a) average margin achieved by tier vs. target margin; (b) below-threshold quotation frequency and total margin impact; (c) quotation-to-order conversion rate by tier and by Sales Rep; (d) quotation win/loss analysis: reasons for lost quotations (price too high, competitor won, project cancelled, customer went direct to vendor); (e) price realization analysis: quoted price vs. invoiced price variance (identifies manual overrides at order stage); (f) report shared with B2B Sales Manager, Category Managers, and VP Merchandising
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager / VP Merchandising
Duration: 3–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W598_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W598_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W598_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W598_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W598_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-274 (ensure controlled execution — Wholesale Operations (PA-11.3).) | - operational: W85 landed cost tracking, monthly price list review, and clear minimum margin floors with approval gates; operational: dedicated government procurement specialist per W78 and pre-bid pricing analysis; operational: requiring reseller commitment indicators (e.g., deposit, LOI) for large quotations and conversion-rate tracking by Sales Rep
Owner: B2B Sales Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W598_Assoc18" sourceRef="W598_Annotation17" targetRef="W598_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W598_Flow19" sourceRef="W598_Start7" targetRef="W598_Task8" />
