    <bpmn:process id="W_W599" name="W599. Wholesale Returns, Credit &amp; Adjustment Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Reseller submits return request; quality issue identified post-delivery; pricing/quantity discrepancy on invoice; vendor-caused defect requiring chargeback
Frequency: ~40–60 wholesale returns/month; ~80–100 credit memos/month (including adjustments for pricing errors, quantity variances, and damaged goods)
Volume: B2B return rate ~1.5–2% of wholesale revenue (vs. ~3–5% for consumer retail); average wholesale return value PHP 15,000–50,000 per transaction (significantly higher than consumer returns due to bulk quantities); return reasons: quality defect (30%), wrong item delivered (20%), quantity discrepancy (15%), overstock/excess (15%), pricing error (10%), damaged in transit (10%)
Owner: B2B Sales Manager
Participants: Sales Representative, B2B Sales Manager, DC Receiving Supervisor (R for goods receipt), Quality Inspector, AR Clerk (R for credit memo), Tax Accountant (R for EWT adjustment), AP Clerk (R for vendor chargeback), Credit Analyst (I for account impact)
Source: workflow W599 — Wholesale Returns, Credit &amp; Adjustment Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W599_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W599_Lane1" name="Sales Representative">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W599_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W599_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W599_Lane2" name="B2B Sales Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W599_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W599_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W599_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W599_Lane3" name="DC Receiving Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W599_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W599_Lane4" name="Quality Inspector">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W599_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W599_Lane5" name="AR Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W599_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W599_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W599_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W599_Lane6" name="Tax Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W599_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W599_End19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W599_Start8" name="Reseller submits return request; quality issue identified post-delivery; pricing/quantity…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W599_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W599_Task9" name="Return request intake">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Return request intake: reseller submits return request via B2B portal, email, or Sales Rep — (a) reseller provides: original Sales Order/Invoice number, item codes, quantities, reason for return (quality defect, wrong item, quantity discrepancy, overstock, pricing error, damaged in transit), photos of defect/damage if applicable; (b) system validates: original invoice exists, return is within return policy window (wholesale return window: 30 days from delivery, except quality defects which have 90-day window), items match original invoice; (c) system creates Return Authorization (RA) request with unique RA number, linked to original invoice and Sales Order
Responsible (R): Sales Representative / Reseller
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: 15–20 min per return request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W599_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W599_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W599_Task10" name="Return authorization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Return authorization: B2B Sales Manager reviews and approves/denies RA request — (a) verify return reason and supporting evidence; (b) for quality defects: verify complaint is consistent with known quality issues for the SKU (cross-reference W110 supplier quality records); (c) for overstock returns: check if return is allowed under reseller agreement (some wholesale contracts limit overstock returns to 5% of purchases per quarter); (d) for pricing errors: verify original quotation vs. invoiced price — if pricing error confirmed, may process credit memo without physical return; (e) if approved: RA issued with return shipping instructions (reseller delivers to nearest DC) and expected credit memo amount (subject to inspection); (f) if denied: Sales Rep communicates denial reason to reseller with escalation option to the B2B Head of Trade / Account Management
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10–15 min per RA</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W599_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W599_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W599_Task11" name="Goods receipt at DC">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Goods receipt at DC: reseller delivers returned goods to designated DC — (a) DC Receiving Supervisor checks returned goods against RA: item codes, quantities, packaging condition; (b) for quality defect returns: DC Supervisor does not accept goods into regular inventory — goods placed in quarantine/returns area per W219 pending quality inspection; (c) for overstock/wrong item returns (goods in resalable condition): DC Supervisor accepts into returns staging area for restocking assessment; (d) DC Supervisor records goods receipt in system: actual quantities received vs. RA quantities; (e) any quantity discrepancy (received less than authorized): documented, credit memo adjusted accordingly
Responsible (R): DC Receiving Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 30–60 min per return receipt (bulk quantities require forklift and staging)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W599_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W599_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W599_Task12" name="Quality inspection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quality inspection: for quality defect and damaged-in-transit returns — (a) Quality Inspector examines returned goods: verify defect matches described reason, assess if defect is manufacturing quality (vendor-caused), handling damage (BuildRight-caused), or customer-caused (reseller mishandling); (b) for vendor-caused defects: initiate vendor chargeback process (step 8) in parallel with customer credit memo; (c) for BuildRight-caused damage (occurred during DC picking or delivery): full credit to reseller, internal root cause investigation per W507; (d) for customer-caused damage: deny credit memo or apply restocking fee, Sales Rep negotiates with reseller; (e) Quality Inspector records findings in system with photos, classification, and recommendation (restock, refurbish, scrap, or RTV per W88)
Responsible (R): Quality Inspector
Accountable (A): Quality Manager
Duration: 15–30 min per return (depends on item complexity)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W599_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W599_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W599_Task13" name="Credit memo computation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Credit memo computation: AR Clerk computes credit memo based on inspection results — (a) full credit: goods returned in resalable condition or BuildRight-caused defect — credit = original invoiced price × quantity returned; (b) restocking fee: for overstock returns in resalable condition — credit = original invoiced price × quantity × (1 − restocking fee %); restocking fee schedule: 5% for standard items, 10% for bulky items (cement, lumber, tiles), 15% for custom/special-order items; (c) partial credit: goods returned with minor damage but usable — credit = original price × quantity × condition discount (negotiated per inspection); (d) no credit: goods returned with customer-caused damage beyond resalability — reseller notified, goods disposed per W91; (e) all credits computed exclusive of VAT — credit memo will add VAT credit separately; (f) system auto-calculates EWT adjustment: if original sale had 1% EWT withheld by reseller, credit memo reduces the taxable base, and reseller must adjust their EWT records accordingly
Responsible (R): AR Clerk
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: 15–20 min per credit memo</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W599_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W599_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W599_Task14" name="BIR-compliant credit note issuance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: BIR-compliant credit note issuance: AR Clerk generates BIR-registered credit note — (a) system generates credit note with: BIR-registered serial number, BuildRight TIN, reseller TIN, original Sales Invoice number and date, original Sales Invoice amount, credit amount, VAT adjustment, reason for credit (BIR requires specific reason codes), credit note date; (b) credit note must be issued within the same month as the return or the following month to comply with BIR invoicing rules; (c) credit note printed on BIR-registered form or issued as BIR-registered electronic credit note (if BuildRight is authorized for e-invoicing per BIR Revenue Regulations); (d) credit note transmitted to reseller via B2B portal or email; (e) system updates AR subledger: credit memo applied against reseller&#x27;s outstanding balance per W8
Responsible (R): AR Clerk / System
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 10–15 min per credit note</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W599_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W599_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W599_Task15" name="EWT adjustment processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: EWT adjustment processing: Tax Accountant processes the EWT implications of the credit memo — (a) original sale: reseller withheld 1% EWT and issued BIR Form 2307 to BuildRight; (b) credit memo reduces the sale amount: the EWT base is now lower; (c) two treatment options: (i) if credit memo and original sale are in the same BIR quarterly return period: net the credit against the sale in the quarterly 1702Q filing — no separate EWT adjustment needed; (ii) if credit memo is in a later period than the original sale: reseller should issue a revised BIR Form 2307 reflecting the reduced purchase amount, and BuildRight adjusts its EWT credit claim in the applicable return period; (d) Tax Accountant notifies reseller of EWT adjustment requirement via Sales Rep; (e) for resellers who are non-compliant with EWT obligations: Credit Analyst notes in account file for W145 credit review
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 10–15 min per adjustment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W599_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W599_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W599_Task16" name="Vendor chargeback if vendor-caused">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Vendor chargeback if vendor-caused: if quality inspection determined defect is vendor-caused — (a) B2B Sales Manager initiates vendor chargeback per W88 RTV process: (i) vendor notified of quality defect with inspection report and photos; (ii) vendor requested to accept return goods or provide replacement; (iii) BuildRight issues debit note to vendor for cost of defective goods + handling/restocking cost; (b) in parallel: customer credit memo (step 6) is issued to reseller based on selling price; vendor debit note (chargeback) is based on BuildRight&#x27;s purchase cost from vendor; (c) difference between customer credit memo amount and vendor chargeback amount = BuildRight&#x27;s margin loss on the transaction (tracked for W44 vendor performance scorecard impact); (d) vendor chargeback processed through AP per W7 as a deduction from next vendor payment
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager / AP Clerk
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 20–30 min per vendor chargeback</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W599_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W599_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W599_Task17" name="AR account adjustment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: AR account adjustment: AR Clerk applies credit memo to reseller&#x27;s AR account — (a) if reseller has outstanding invoices: credit memo applied against oldest outstanding invoice first (FIFO application) or against specific invoice per reseller request; (b) if reseller has no outstanding balance: credit memo becomes a credit balance on account — applied against next invoice automatically or refunded per reseller request; (c) for credit balance refunds (reseller requests cash refund of credit balance): process per W7 payment run with B2B Sales Manager approval; (d) system updates AR aging per W70 — credit memos aged from credit memo date, not original invoice date; (e) credit memo reflected in monthly customer statement per W100
Responsible (R): AR Clerk
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: 5–10 min per application</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W599_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W599_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W599_Task18" name="Monthly wholesale return analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Monthly wholesale return analytics: B2B Sales Manager reviews monthly return and credit memo data — (a) return rate by reseller: identify resellers with return rate &gt;3% (above average) for review; (b) return reason distribution: track shifts in return reasons over time; (c) vendor-caused returns: aggregate by vendor for W44 vendor performance review; (d) restocking fee revenue vs. restocking cost: verify restocking fees cover actual labor, inspection, and repackaging costs; (e) credit memo aging per W70: identify aged credit memos not applied to invoices; (f) BIR credit note compliance: verify all credit notes issued within required timeframe; (g) feed findings into W110 supplier quality and W44 vendor performance reviews
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W599_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W599_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W599_End19" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W599_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W599_Annotation20">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-274 (ensure controlled execution — Wholesale Operations (PA-11.3).) | - operational: system-generated BIR-compliant credit notes (step 6) and monthly compliance review (step 10); operational: Tax Accountant follow-up and building EWT adjustment requirements into wholesale contracts per W145; operational: rejecting returns of bulk commodities where packaging is compromised and escalating restocking fees for high-cost-to-handle items
Owner: B2B Sales Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W599_Assoc21" sourceRef="W599_Annotation20" targetRef="W599_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W599_Flow22" sourceRef="W599_Start8" targetRef="W599_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W599_Flow23" sourceRef="W599_Task9" targetRef="W599_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W599_Flow24" sourceRef="W599_Task10" targetRef="W599_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W599_Flow25" sourceRef="W599_Task11" targetRef="W599_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W599_Flow26" sourceRef="W599_Task12" targetRef="W599_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W599_Flow27" sourceRef="W599_Task13" targetRef="W599_Task14" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W599_Flow28" sourceRef="W599_Task14" targetRef="W599_Task15" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W599_Flow29" sourceRef="W599_Task15" targetRef="W599_Task16" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W599_Flow30" sourceRef="W599_Task16" targetRef="W599_Task17" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W599_Flow31" sourceRef="W599_Task17" targetRef="W599_Task18" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W599_Flow32" sourceRef="W599_Task18" targetRef="W599_End19" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W599_diag">
