    <bpmn:process id="W_W704" name="W704. Wholesale Customer Contract Renewal &amp; Tier Reclassification" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual contract renewal cycle; quarterly tier review; customer volume change (significant increase or decrease); customer credit event; strategic partnership review
Frequency: Annual contract renewals (~100–150); quarterly tier assessments; ad-hoc for credit events or strategic changes
Volume: ~100–150 active wholesale reseller contracts; ~30–50 contract renewals/year; ~20–30 tier changes/year
Owner: B2B Sales Manager
Participants: Credit Analyst (credit review), Finance Manager (margin analysis), Category Manager (pricing approval), VP Merchandising (strategic accounts), Legal (contract terms)
Source: workflow W704 — Wholesale Customer Contract Renewal &amp; Tier Reclassification</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W704_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W704_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W704_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W704_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W704_Lane2" name="B2B Sales Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W704_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W704_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W704_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W704_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W704_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W704_Lane3" name="Credit Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W704_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W704_Lane4" name="Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W704_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W704_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W704_Start6" name="Annual contract renewal cycle; quarterly tier review; customer volume change (significant…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W704_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W704_Task7" name="Annual contract renewal initiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual contract renewal initiation: 90 days before contract expiry, system auto-generates renewal reminder to B2B Sales Manager: (a) contract summary: current tier, annual purchase volume, average margin, payment behavior, credit utilization; (b) system recommends renewal action based on trailing 12-month data: Continue (if performance satisfactory), Renegotiate (if margin or payment issues), Upgrade tier (if volume exceeds current tier threshold), Downgrade tier (if volume below threshold), Non-renew (if chronic issues per step 2)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W704_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W704_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W704_Task8" name="Customer performance review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Customer performance review: B2B Sales Manager evaluates each wholesale customer: (a) trailing 12-month purchase volume vs. tier threshold (Bronze &lt;PHP 5M, Silver PHP 5-15M, Gold PHP 15-30M, Platinum &gt;PHP 30M per W598); (b) payment behavior: average days to pay, number of overdue invoices, bad debt history; (c) return rate: is return rate within acceptable range (&lt;3%) or excessive per W599 analytics; (d) margin contribution: average margin on sales to this customer; (e) strategic value: is this customer in a growth market, do they carry complementary products, do they refer other customers; (f) competitive situation: is this customer at risk of switching to a competitor
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30-60 min per customer</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W704_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W704_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W704_Task9" name="Credit review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Credit review: Credit Analyst conducts annual credit review: (a) request updated financial statements from reseller; (b) verify BIR registration and tax compliance (current 2303 certificate); (c) review trade references and payment history; (d) recommend: maintain credit limit, increase credit limit (for customers with strong payment history and growth), decrease credit limit (for customers with deteriorating payment behavior), or suspend credit (require prepayment)
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 1-3 days per customer (externally driven)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W704_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W704_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W704_Task10" name="Tier reclassification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Tier reclassification: based on performance and credit review: (a) tier upgrade: customer&#x27;s trailing 12-month volume qualifies for next tier — apply upgraded pricing, update customer master per W508, communicate upgrade benefits to customer; (b) tier downgrade: customer&#x27;s trailing 12-month volume falls below tier threshold — B2B Sales Manager reviews: if temporary (customer between projects): grant 1-quarter grace period at current tier; if permanent decline: downgrade to appropriate tier, communicate change with 30-day notice, offer retention options (project pricing to bridge volume gap); (c) tier change requires Category Manager approval for margin impact assessment
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15-30 min per tier change</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W704_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W704_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W704_Task11" name="Contract renewal negotiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Contract renewal negotiation: B2B Sales Manager contacts customer for renewal discussion: (a) present performance review and tier decision; (b) negotiate terms: pricing tier, credit terms, minimum purchase commitment, exclusivity provisions (if applicable), marketing support (co-branded campaigns); (c) for key strategic accounts (top 20 by volume): VP Merchandising participates in renewal discussion; (d) document agreed terms for contract update
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1-2 hours per customer</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W704_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W704_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W704_Task12" name="Contract update and execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Contract update and execution: (a) Legal updates contract per W688 with agreed terms: pricing tier, credit limit, payment terms, delivery terms, minimum purchase commitment, termination clause, EWT provisions per BIR requirements; (b) route for approval per DOA: standard contracts — B2B Sales Manager + Legal; high-value accounts — VP Merchandising + CFO; (c) execute via digital signature per W686 or physical signature if customer requires; (d) register renewed contract in CLM system per W688; (e) update customer master and pricing in ERP
Responsible (R): Legal / B2B Sales Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1-3 days per contract</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W704_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W704_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W704_Task13" name="Non-renewal and account closure">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Non-renewal and account closure: for customers not renewed: (a) B2B Sales Manager issues non-renewal notice per contract terms (typically 30-60 days before expiry); (b) ensure all outstanding invoices collected per W8; (c) revoke B2B portal access and punchout catalog access per W283; (d) de-activate wholesale account in customer master per W508; (e) Finance verifies no outstanding credit memos or unapplied payments
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager / Finance
Accountable (A): Legal
Duration: 1-2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W704_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W704_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W704_Task14" name="Annual portfolio review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Annual portfolio review: B2B Sales Manager presents annual wholesale portfolio review to VP Merchandising and CFO: (a) portfolio composition by tier (count of customers and revenue by tier); (b) tier migration summary (how many upgraded/downgraded/non-renewed); (c) revenue retention rate (% of revenue renewed vs. churned); (d) average margin by tier and trend; (e) new customer acquisition vs. lost customers; (f) competitive landscape changes; (g) recommendations for next year&#x27;s wholesale strategy
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising / CFO
Duration: 1 day/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W704_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W704_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W704_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W704_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W704_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-274 (ensure controlled execution — Wholesale Operations (PA-11.3).) | - operational: B2B Sales Manager review and approval gate
Owner: B2B Sales Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W704_Assoc17" sourceRef="W704_Annotation16" targetRef="W704_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
