    <bpmn:process id="W_W809" name="W809. Wholesale Consignment Inventory Management &amp; Settlement" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Strategic reseller agreement includes consignment terms; new product launch requiring market seeding; seasonal inventory push to key reseller locations
Frequency: ~10–15 consignment agreements active at any time; settlement cycles monthly or per agreement terms
Volume: ~5% of wholesale revenue (~PHP 935M annually) on consignment; primarily seasonal items (paint during summer, cement during construction peak), new product launches, and slow-moving inventory pushed to reseller shelves
Owner: B2B Sales Manager
Participants: Sales Representative, B2B Sales Manager, Reseller (R for sell-through reporting), Finance Analyst (R for settlement), AR Clerk (R for invoicing), DC Inventory Controller (R for consignment stock tracking)
Source: workflow W809 — Wholesale Consignment Inventory Management &amp; Settlement</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W809_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W809_Lane1" name="B2B Sales Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W809_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W809_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W809_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W809_Lane2" name="Sales Representative">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W809_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W809_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W809_Lane3" name="Reseller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W809_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W809_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W809_Lane4" name="Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W809_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W809_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W809_Start6" name="Strategic reseller agreement includes consignment terms; new product launch requiring…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W809_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W809_Task7" name="Consignment agreement setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Consignment agreement setup: B2B Sales Manager negotiates consignment terms with reseller: (a) product scope: specific SKUs eligible for consignment (typically 10–30 SKUs per agreement); (b) consignment quantity: initial stock level and replenishment trigger point; (c) settlement period: monthly sell-through settlement (standard) or per-agreement terms; (d) pricing: consignment selling price to reseller (typically same as wholesale tier price per W598); (e) payment terms: reseller pays for sold goods within 15 days of settlement report; (f) physical count: reseller agrees to monthly physical count or BuildRight audit count; (g) loss/damage responsibility: reseller liable for loss or damage beyond normal shelf wear; (h) agreement documented per W688 contract lifecycle and added to customer master per W508
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager / Legal
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 days per agreement</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W809_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W809_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W809_Task8" name="Initial consignment shipment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Initial consignment shipment: DC fulfills consignment order per W146 bulk fulfillment: (a) Sales Representative creates consignment Sales Order in ERP with &quot;Consignment&quot; flag; (b) system does not create AR invoice at shipment — ownership has not transferred; (c) system moves inventory from DC stock to &quot;Consignment — [Reseller Name]&quot; virtual location in inventory module; (d) goods shipped and delivered per W146 with consignment delivery receipt (not invoice); (e) reseller signs Consignment Receipt acknowledging quantity received and custodial responsibility
Responsible (R): Sales Representative / DC Team
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: Per W146 timeline</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W809_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W809_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W809_Task9" name="Sell-through reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Sell-through reporting: Reseller reports sales of consignment goods: (a) standard process: reseller submits monthly sell-through report via B2B portal — item codes, quantities sold, selling price to end customer, date of sale; (b) automated process (for resellers with POS integration per W283): system receives daily sell-through data feed; (c) Sales Rep follows up with reseller by 5th business day of month if sell-through report not submitted; (d) system reconciles: opening consignment balance + shipments during period − reported sales = expected closing consignment balance
Responsible (R): Reseller / Sales Representative
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: Monthly (reseller: 30–60 min; Sales Rep follow-up: 15–30 min)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W809_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W809_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W809_Task10" name="Monthly physical count reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Monthly physical count reconciliation: To verify sell-through accuracy and prevent shrinkage: (a) reseller conducts physical count of all consignment SKUs at month-end; (b) physical count compared to system expected balance (from step 3 reconciliation); (c) if variance ≤2%: acceptable — system adjusts inventory to physical count; (d) if variance &gt;2%: Sales Rep conducts on-site audit count within 5 business days; (e) unexplained losses charged to reseller at consignment cost per agreement terms; (f) quarterly: BuildRight DC Inventory Controller performs surprise audit count at top 5 consignment locations by value
Responsible (R): Reseller / Sales Representative / DC Inventory Controller
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours per count (reseller); 2–4 hours per audit (BuildRight)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W809_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W809_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W809_Task11" name="Settlement and invoicing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Settlement and invoicing: Based on confirmed sell-through: (a) Finance Analyst generates monthly consignment settlement: itemized list of goods sold during period × consignment price = amount due; (b) system creates AR invoice for sold goods — VAT computed at point of sale; (c) EWT: if reseller is withholding agent, EWT (1%) computed on settlement amount; reseller issues BIR Form 2307 for the settlement period; (d) AR invoice transmitted to reseller via B2B portal; (e) payment collected per W8 within 15-day payment term; (f) inventory records updated: consignment stock reduced by quantity sold
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst / AR Clerk
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2–3 hours per settlement</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W809_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W809_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W809_Task12" name="Consignment replenishment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Consignment replenishment: When consignment stock falls below replenishment trigger: (a) system generates auto-replenishment alert based on sell-through velocity and minimum stock level per agreement; (b) Sales Representative confirms replenishment order with reseller; (c) DC fulfills replenishment per W146; (d) if reseller requests product mix change (e.g., replace slow-moving SKU with faster seller): Sales Rep coordinates with Category Manager for SKU substitution approval; (e) unsold consignment returns: if SKU is being removed from consignment, goods returned to DC per W599 wholesale returns process
Responsible (R): Sales Representative / DC Team
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: Per W146 timeline for fulfillment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W809_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W809_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W809_Task13" name="Consignment aging and review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Consignment aging and review: Quarterly, B2B Sales Manager reviews consignment portfolio: (a) aging analysis: consignment stock held &gt;90 days without sell-through flagged for review; (b) slow-moving consignment SKUs: identify SKUs with &lt;30% sell-through rate — discuss with Category Manager for markdown, return, or replacement; (c) consignment profitability: margin analysis per consignment agreement — factoring in carrying cost, handling cost, and loss/damage rate; (d) reseller consignment performance: identify resellers with low sell-through rates, high loss rates, or late settlements for agreement renegotiation or termination; (e) total consignment exposure: aggregate consignment inventory value across all agreements — compare to approved exposure limit per VP Merchandising
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager / Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W809_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W809_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W809_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W809_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W809_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-274 (ensure controlled execution — Wholesale Operations (PA-11.3).) | - operational: monthly physical counts, quarterly surprise audits, and contractual loss liability allocation (step 1g and step 4e); operational: system-driven VAT computation based on settled sell-through data (step 5); operational: automated B2B portal reporting, Sales Rep follow-up (step 3c), and contractual penalties for late reporting
Owner: B2B Sales Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W809_Assoc16" sourceRef="W809_Annotation15" targetRef="W809_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W809_Flow17" sourceRef="W809_Start6" targetRef="W809_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W809_Flow18" sourceRef="W809_Task7" targetRef="W809_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W809_Flow19" sourceRef="W809_Task8" targetRef="W809_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W809_Flow20" sourceRef="W809_Task9" targetRef="W809_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W809_Flow21" sourceRef="W809_Task10" targetRef="W809_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W809_Flow22" sourceRef="W809_Task11" targetRef="W809_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W809_Flow23" sourceRef="W809_Task12" targetRef="W809_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W809_Flow24" sourceRef="W809_Task13" targetRef="W809_End14" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W809_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W809_plane" bpmnElement="W_W809">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W809_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W809_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1790" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W809_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W809_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1790" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W809_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W809_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1790" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W809_Lane4_di" bpmnElement="W809_Lane4" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="590" width="1790" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W809_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W809_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W809_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W809_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W809_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W809_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W809_Task10_di" bpmnElement="W809_Task10"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W809_Task11_di" bpmnElement="W809_Task11"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="635" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W809_Task12_di" bpmnElement="W809_Task12"><dc:Bounds x="1450" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W809_Task13_di" bpmnElement="W809_Task13"><dc:Bounds x="1660" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W809_Start6_di" bpmnElement="W809_Start6"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W809_End14_di" bpmnElement="W809_End14"><dc:Bounds x="1890" y="657" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W809_Annotation15_di" bpmnElement="W809_Annotation15"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="800" width="360" height="114" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W809_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W809_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W809_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W809_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W809_Flow19_di" bpmnElement="W809_Flow19"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W809_Flow20_di" bpmnElement="W809_Flow20"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W809_Flow21_di" bpmnElement="W809_Flow21"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="675" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W809_Flow22_di" bpmnElement="W809_Flow22"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="675" /><di:waypoint x="1450" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
