    <bpmn:process id="W_W810" name="W810. Wholesale Backorder Management, Allocation &amp; Customer Communication" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Wholesale Sales Order contains items not available in DC inventory; vendor delivery delay causes stockout for committed wholesale orders; allocation conflict between wholesale and retail channels
Frequency: ~15–24 wholesale orders/month contain backordered items (~15–20% of the ~80–120 wholesale orders/month)
Volume: ~100–150 active resellers; ~80–120 wholesale orders/month; commodity items (cement, steel, plywood) most prone to backorder due to supply volatility
Owner: B2B Sales Manager
Participants: Sales Representative, B2B Sales Manager, DC Inventory Planner, Category Manager (A for allocation), Supply Chain Planner, Reseller (I)
Source: workflow W810 — Wholesale Backorder Management, Allocation &amp; Customer Communication</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W810_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W810_Lane1" name="Sales Representative">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W810_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W810_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W810_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W810_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W810_Lane2" name="DC Inventory Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W810_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W810_Lane3" name="Supply Chain Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W810_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W810_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W810_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W810_Lane5" name="B2B Sales Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W810_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W810_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W810_Start7" name="Wholesale Sales Order contains items not available in DC inventory; vendor delivery delay…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W810_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W810_Task8" name="Backorder identification at order entry">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Backorder identification at order entry: When Sales Representative enters wholesale order: (a) system checks DC inventory per SKU per W146; (b) if item not available at DC: system flags line as &quot;Backorder&quot; with estimated replenishment date from W31 supply plan; (c) system checks alternate DCs: if available at another DC, offer cross-DC transfer per W34 or direct ship from alternate DC per W146; (d) if item not available at any DC: system checks vendor purchase order pipeline — if PO already placed with confirmed delivery date, system provides estimated availability; (e) Sales Representative presents options to reseller: (i) split delivery — ship available items now, backordered items upon replenishment; (ii) hold entire order until all items available; (iii) substitute items per W16 product substitution rules; (iv) cancel backordered line items
Responsible (R): Sales Representative / System
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: 15–20 min per order with backorders</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W810_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W810_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W810_Task9" name="Allocation priority determination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Allocation priority determination: When available inventory is insufficient to fulfill all demand (wholesale + retail): (a) DC Inventory Planner runs allocation analysis: total available stock vs. total open orders (wholesale + retail + ecommerce); (b) allocation priority rules applied: (i) committed orders (accepted quotation converted to SO per W598 step 7) take priority over uncommitted quotations; (ii) Platinum/Gold tier resellers per W598 take priority over Bronze/Silver for the same SKU; (iii) government procurement orders per W78 take priority (contractual delivery penalties); (iv) project-critical orders (reseller provides documented project deadline) take priority over standard replenishment orders; (v) retail and ecommerce channels allocated remaining stock after priority wholesale fulfillment; (c) if allocation rules produce an unfair result (e.g., a small Bronze reseller with a hospital construction deadline loses allocation to a large Platinum reseller doing routine restocking): B2B Sales Manager may override with Category Manager approval
Responsible (R): DC Inventory Planner / B2B Sales Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 30–60 min per allocation conflict</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W810_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W810_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W810_Task10" name="Customer communication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer communication: Sales Representative proactively communicates backorder status to reseller: (a) initial notification: within 4 hours of order entry, Sales Rep sends backorder notification via B2B portal and email — backordered items, estimated availability, reseller&#x27;s selected delivery option (split, hold, substitute, cancel); (b) weekly status update: for backorders lasting &gt;7 days, system auto-generates weekly status update with revised estimated availability; (c) vendor delay notification: if vendor confirms delivery delay, Sales Representative immediately notifies affected resellers with revised timeline; (d) allocation notification: if reseller&#x27;s order is partially allocated due to scarcity, Sales Rep explains allocation rationale and offers alternatives
Responsible (R): Sales Representative / System
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: 10–15 min per communication</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W810_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W810_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W810_Task11" name="Expedited replenishment for critical backorders">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Expedited replenishment for critical backorders: For high-priority backorders (Platinum/Gold tier, government procurement, project-critical): (a) Supply Chain Planner contacts vendor for expedited production or delivery; (b) if vendor can expedite: additional freight cost (air freight, special delivery) may apply — B2B Sales Manager approves incremental cost if margin remains above floor per W598; (c) if vendor cannot expedite: Supply Chain Planner checks alternative vendors per W3 approved vendor list; (d) if alternative sourcing found: Category Manager approves alternative vendor and any price differential; (e) if no expedited solution: B2B Sales Manager communicates revised timeline to reseller with mitigation options (partial delivery, project phasing support)
Responsible (R): Supply Chain Planner / Category Manager
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: 1–3 hours per critical backorder</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W810_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W810_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W810_Task12" name="Backorder-to-delivery conversion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Backorder-to-delivery conversion: When backordered stock arrives at DC: (a) system automatically allocates received stock against open backorders per allocation priority (step 2); (b) system generates pick task for DC per W146; (c) Sales Representative notified that backorder is ready for shipment; (d) if reseller previously selected split delivery: only backordered items shipped in this delivery; (e) if reseller previously selected hold: entire order now shipped; (f) system sends shipment confirmation to reseller with expected delivery date
Responsible (R): System / DC Team / Sales Representative
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: Automated + 15 min per order</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W810_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W810_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W810_Task13" name="Backorder cancellation and expiration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Backorder cancellation and expiration: If backorder cannot be fulfilled within agreed timeframe: (a) standard backorder validity: 30 days from original order date; (b) for commodity items with known supply disruption: extended to 60 days with reseller consent; (c) at expiry: system alerts Sales Representative to contact reseller — extend, cancel, or substitute; (d) if reseller cancels: system cancels backorder line, releases any allocated stock, updates order total; (e) if reseller does not respond within 5 business days of expiry notification: system auto-cancels backorder line; (f) cancelled backorder lines with previously collected deposit: refund processed per W599 credit memo process
Responsible (R): Sales Representative / System
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: 10 min per cancellation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W810_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W810_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W810_Task14" name="Monthly backorder analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monthly backorder analytics: B2B Sales Manager reviews monthly backorder performance: (a) backorder rate: % of wholesale order lines backordered — target &lt;10%; (b) average backorder fulfillment time by SKU and vendor; (c) backorder-to-cancellation rate: % of backorders that expire or are cancelled — lost revenue analysis; (d) vendor reliability: which vendors cause the most backorders — feed into W44 vendor performance scorecard; (e) channel allocation fairness: review allocation overrides for equity; (f) customer satisfaction impact: track reseller complaints and churn correlated with backorder frequency
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager / DC Inventory Planner
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 3–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W810_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W810_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W810_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W810_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W810_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-274 (ensure controlled execution — Wholesale Operations (PA-11.3).) | - operational: structured allocation priority rules (step 2) with override approval; operational: safety stock buffers per W31 and dual-sourcing per W3; operational: realistic delivery commitments at quotation stage per W598 and expedited replenishment (step 4)
Owner: B2B Sales Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W810_Assoc17" sourceRef="W810_Annotation16" targetRef="W810_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W810_Flow18" sourceRef="W810_Start7" targetRef="W810_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W810_Flow19" sourceRef="W810_Task8" targetRef="W810_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W810_Flow20" sourceRef="W810_Task9" targetRef="W810_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W810_Flow21" sourceRef="W810_Task10" targetRef="W810_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W810_Flow22" sourceRef="W810_Task11" targetRef="W810_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W810_Flow23" sourceRef="W810_Task12" targetRef="W810_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W810_Flow24" sourceRef="W810_Task13" targetRef="W810_Task14" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W810_Flow25" sourceRef="W810_Task14" targetRef="W810_End15" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W810_diag">
