    <bpmn:process id="W_W811" name="W811. Wholesale Delivery Proof, Discrepancy Resolution &amp; POD Reconciliation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Wholesale delivery completed; reseller reports quantity or quality discrepancy on delivery; POD document not returned; invoice-to-delivery mismatch identified during AR reconciliation
Frequency: ~50–100 wholesale deliveries/week across 4 DCs; ~10–15% of deliveries have some form of discrepancy (quantity, damage, wrong item)
Volume: ~2,500–5,000 wholesale deliveries/year; ~300–750 delivery discrepancies/year requiring resolution
Owner: B2B Sales Manager
Participants: Driver (R for POD), DC Dispatcher, Reseller Receiving Clerk, Sales Representative, B2B Sales Manager, AR Clerk, Quality Inspector (R for quality discrepancies), Finance Analyst (R for reconciliation)
Source: workflow W811 — Wholesale Delivery Proof, Discrepancy Resolution &amp; POD Reconciliation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W811_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W811_Lane1" name="Driver">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W811_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W811_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W811_Lane2" name="DC Dispatcher">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W811_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W811_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W811_Lane3" name="Sales Representative">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W811_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W811_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W811_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W811_Lane5" name="Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W811_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W811_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W811_Start7" name="Wholesale delivery completed; reseller reports quantity or quality discrepancy on…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W811_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W811_Task8" name="Delivery and POD capture">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Delivery and POD capture: At point of delivery per W146: (a) driver presents Delivery Receipt (DR) to reseller receiving clerk; (b) reseller and driver jointly verify delivery: (i) check seal integrity on sealed shipments; (ii) verify pallet count and visual condition; (iii) for bulk commodities (cement, steel): weight check at reseller&#x27;s scale or driver&#x27;s scale ticket; (iv) for counted items: tally count against DR line items; (c) reseller notes any discrepancies on DR: quantity shortage, visible damage, wrong item, missing items; (d) if discrepancy found: driver and reseller both note discrepancy on DR with quantities, item codes, and description of issue; both sign the annotated DR; (e) if no discrepancy: reseller signs DR as &quot;Received in good order and correct quantity&quot;; (f) driver captures POD via mobile app: photo of signed DR, GPS coordinates, timestamp; (g) for resellers requiring BIR 2307 (EWT): driver collects signed BIR 2307 from reseller or notes that 2307 will be mailed
Responsible (R): Driver / Reseller Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): DC Dispatcher
Duration: 20–45 min per delivery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W811_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W811_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W811_Task9" name="POD return and system recording">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: POD return and system recording: (a) driver returns signed POD/DR to DC Dispatcher at end of delivery run (or POD transmitted in real-time via mobile app); (b) DC Dispatcher records POD in system: delivery confirmed, any discrepancies noted, signed DR scanned and attached to Sales Order; (c) system matches POD to Sales Order and triggers: if POD matches SO (no discrepancy): auto-trigger billing per step 5; if POD has discrepancy: route to discrepancy resolution per step 3; if POD not returned within 48 hours of delivery: system alerts DC Dispatcher and Sales Representative for follow-up
Responsible (R): DC Dispatcher / System
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 10–15 min per POD</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W811_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W811_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W811_Task10" name="Discrepancy triage and classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Discrepancy triage and classification: Sales Representative and DC Dispatcher review delivery discrepancy: (a) quantity shortage: driver delivered less than DR quantity — (i) check DC pick records: was correct quantity picked? (ii) check loading tally: was correct quantity loaded? (iii) check driver route: any intermediate stops or evidence of pilferage? (iv) if DC error: acknowledge shortage, issue credit memo per W599 for undelivered quantity; (v) if transit loss/pilferage: file insurance claim per W610 and issue credit memo; (b) quantity excess: driver delivered more than DR quantity — (i) verify against Sales Order: if excess matches SO, update DR and bill for full SO quantity; (ii) if excess exceeds SO: arrange return pickup or treat as complimentary sample per W69; (c) damage during transit: (i) driver and reseller document damage with photos at delivery; (ii) if minor damage (packaging only, product intact): accept delivery, note condition, no credit needed; (iii) if significant damage (product unusable): reject damaged items at delivery, return to DC, credit memo per W599, insurance claim per W610; (d) wrong item delivered: (i) reseller rejects wrong items at delivery; (ii) wrong items returned to DC on same truck or next delivery; (iii) correct items shipped on priority basis; (iv) root cause analysis at DC picking per W262
Responsible (R): Sales Representative / DC Dispatcher
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: 30–60 min per discrepancy</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W811_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W811_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W811_Task11" name="Unresolved POD follow-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Unresolved POD follow-up: For deliveries where POD is not returned or is disputed: (a) POD not returned within 48 hours: (i) DC Dispatcher contacts driver for POD; (ii) if driver cannot provide: Sales Representative contacts reseller to confirm delivery verbally; (iii) if reseller confirms delivery: system records verbal confirmation (weaker than signed POD but sufficient for billing); (iv) if reseller does not confirm: escalate to B2B Sales Manager for investigation; (b) POD disputed by reseller (reseller claims they did not receive, or received less than DR): (i) system pulls GPS record from driver mobile app and in-cab dashcam footage if available; (ii) system checks weight bridge records if applicable; (iii) DC pick and loading records reviewed; (iv) B2B Sales Manager mediates between driver, DC, and reseller; (v) if unresolved: insurance claim for loss, credit memo to reseller, driver disciplinary action if negligence determined
Responsible (R): DC Dispatcher / Sales Representative / B2B Sales Manager
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 1–3 hours per unresolved POD</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W811_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W811_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W811_Task12" name="Three-way match and billing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Three-way match and billing: System performs three-way match before AR invoice generation: (a) Sales Order (what was ordered); (b) Delivery Receipt/POD (what was delivered and accepted); (c) AR Invoice (what will be billed); (d) if SO = POD: invoice generated for full SO amount — standard process; (e) if POD &lt; SO (shortage): invoice generated for POD quantity only; remaining SO quantity either backordered per W810 or cancelled; (f) if POD &gt; SO (excess): invoice adjusted per step 3b resolution; (g) if POD has quality discrepancy: invoice adjusted per step 3c resolution; (h) invoice transmitted to reseller via B2B portal with POD attachment for reseller&#x27;s records; (i) system updates AR subledger per W8 with invoice and payment terms
Responsible (R): System / AR Clerk
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Automated + 10 min per discrepancy adjustment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W811_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W811_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W811_Task13" name="Monthly POD reconciliation and analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly POD reconciliation and analytics: Finance Analyst conducts monthly reconciliation: (a) POD return rate: % of deliveries with signed POD returned within 48 hours — target &gt;95%; (b) discrepancy rate by type: quantity shortage, quantity excess, damage, wrong item; (c) discrepancy rate by DC, driver, and product category; (d) average time from delivery to invoice (billing lag) — target &lt;3 business days for clean deliveries; (e) unresolved POD aging: deliveries without confirmed POD &gt;30 days — escalate to B2B Sales Manager; (f) insurance claims filed per W610 for transit losses; (g) driver performance scorecard feed for repeat discrepancy drivers; (h) findings shared with B2B Sales Manager, DC Managers, and COO
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst / B2B Sales Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 3–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W811_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W811_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W811_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W811_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W811_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-274 (ensure controlled execution — Wholesale Operations (PA-11.3).) | - operational: weight bridge records and pallet-level barcoding where feasible; operational: real-time mobile POD capture (step 1f) and 48-hour escalation (step 4a); operational: GPS tracking, sealed shipments, random DC-to-reseller physical audits, and driver rotation
Owner: B2B Sales Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W811_Assoc16" sourceRef="W811_Annotation15" targetRef="W811_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
